      "content": "that sounds nice for a library, but i'm not really thinking about \"atmosphere.\" i mean, if you look at the way the fern fronds are angled toward the seating area and how the large lily leaves are positioned at ear level... it looks way too systematic for just decoration. if someone wanted to capture clear audio from people talking at those desks without using visible microphones, using the plant structure to funnel or focus sound waves toward a central point makes a lot of sense. can you look into whether those specific leaf shapes and the cluster density could actually act like parabolic reflectors for capturing speech?",
